 the payload assertion in `patient-registration.test.tsx` matches `person` exactly rather than partially, so it had to record the three new properties. Without that the existing test fails. It has the side benefit of pinning the new payload at the render-to-request level.\n\nTests cover both levels the ticket asks for: a unit test that the generated payload contains `dead: false` plus the three explicit nulls, and a request-level test asserting on the body actually handed to `savePatient`. Both fail without the fix. The coded and non-coded cause-of-death paths are also covered so the `isDead: true` behaviour stays pinned.\n\n## Screenshots\n\n## Related Issue\n\nhttps://openmrs.atlassian.net/browse/O3-5919\n\n## Other\n\nVerified with `yarn verify` (27/27 tasks), the full registration suite (38 files, 283 passing), `tsc`, `eslint` and a production build. FHIR still represents the patient as not deceased, since `mapPatientToFhirPatient` derives `deceasedBoolean` from `dead`.\n","freshness":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","lastSyncedAt":"2026-10-31T16:11:31.413Z","stale":false}],"nextOffset":null,"truncated":[]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JaDaY7yU1jBKj4DuYgS4fZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
